  "id": "dsa-337",
  "title": "Introduction to Deque - GeeksforGeeks",
  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>A </span><b><strong>Deque (Double-Ended Queue)</strong></b><span> is a linear data structure that allows insertion and deletion of elements from both ends. Unlike a stack or a queue, where operations are restricted to one end, a deque provides flexibility to add or remove elements at the front as well as the rear.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Deque can act as both Stack and Queue</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>It is useful in many problems where we need to have a subset of all operations also like insert/remove at front and insert/remove at the end.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>It is typically implemented either using a doubly linked list or circular array.</span></li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Deque\" height=\"400\" src=\"./images/dsa-337-img-1.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250910175031267287/Deque.webp 801w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250910175031267287/Deque-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250910175031267287/Deque-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250910175031267287/Deque-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250910175031267287/Deque-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250910175031267287/Deque-768.webp 768w\" width=\"801\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><h2 id=\"common-operations-of-deque\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Common Operations of Deque:</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>In order to make manipulations in a deque, there are certain operations provided to us.</span></p><ol><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>insertFront(x)</strong></b><span> → Insert an element at the front end.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><b><strong>insertRear(x)</strong></b><span> → Insert an element at the rear end.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><b><strong>deleteFront()</strong></b><span> → Delete an element from the front end.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><b><strong>deleteRear()</strong></b><span> → Delete an element from the rear end.</span></li><li value=\"5\"><b><strong>getFront()</strong></b><span> → Retrieve (but don’t remove) the front element.</span></li><li value=\"6\"><b><strong>getRear()</strong></b><span> → Retrieve (but don’t remove) the rear element.</span></li><li value=\"7\"><b><strong>isEmpty()</strong></b><span> → Check if the deque is empty.</span></li><li value=\"8\"><b><strong>size()</strong></b><span> → Return the number of elements currently in the deque.</span></li></ol><h3 id=\"code-example\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Code Example </span></h3><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">C++</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"cpp\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-cpp\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;deque&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">std</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">deque</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push_back</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push_back</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">20</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push_front</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">30</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// Print deque elements</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cout</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" \"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">cout</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">endl</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// Pop from front and back</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pop_front</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pop_back</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// Print deque elements after pop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cout</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" \"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">Java</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"java\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-java\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">java.util.ArrayDeque</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">java.util.Deque</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Main</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">Deque</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Integer</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ArrayDeque</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">addLast</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">addLast</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">20</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">addFirst</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">30</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// Print deque elements</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" \"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// Pop from front and back</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">removeFirst</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">removeLast</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// Print deque elements after pop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" \"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">Python</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"python3\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-python3\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kn\">from</span> <span class=\"nn\">collections</span> <span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">deque</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">dq</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">deque</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">append</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">append</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">20</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">appendleft</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">30</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\"># Print deque elements</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">' '</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">join</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">map</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\"># Pop from front and back</span>\n<span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">popleft</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pop</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\"># Print deque elements after pop</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">' '</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">join</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">map</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">C#</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"csharp\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-csharp\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"k\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">System</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">System.Collections.Generic</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">Program</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">Main</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">Deque</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Deque</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AddLast</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">10</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AddLast</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">20</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AddFirst</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">30</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// Print deque elements</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">foreach</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Write</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" \"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">Console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">WriteLine</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// Pop from front and back</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">RemoveFirst</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">RemoveLast</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// Print deque elements after pop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">foreach</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dq</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Write</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" \"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">Deque</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinkedList</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinkedList</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">AddFirst</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">value</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AddFirst</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">value</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">AddLast</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">value</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AddLast</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">value</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">RemoveFirst</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">RemoveFirst</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">RemoveLast</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">RemoveLast</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IEnumerator</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GetEnumerator</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">GetEnumerator</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><div class=\"code-output\"><br><strong>Output</strong><pre>30 10 20 \n10 </pre></div><h2 id=\"implementation-of-stack\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Implementation of Deque:</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>Deque can be implemented in Different Ways :-</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><a href=\"#/article/dsa/dsa-338\"><span>Implementation of Deque Using Array</span></a></li><li value=\"2\"><a href=\"#/article/dsa/dsa-855\"><span>Implementation of Deque Using LinkedList</span></a></li></ul><h3 id=\"advantage-of-deque\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Advantage of Deque:</span></h3><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"advantages_of_deque\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/dsa-337-img-2.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250920183047987413/advantages_of_deque.webp 800w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250920183047987413/advantages_of_deque-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250920183047987413/advantages_of_deque-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250920183047987413/advantages_of_deque-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250920183047987413/advantages_of_deque-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250920183047987413/advantages_of_deque-768.webp 768w\" width=\"800\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure></div>",
  "textContent": "A Deque (Double-Ended Queue) is a linear data structure that allows insertion and deletion of elements from both ends. Unlike a stack or a queue, where operations are restricted to one end, a deque provides flexibility to add or remove elements at the front as well as the rear.Deque can act as both Stack and QueueIt is useful in many problems where we need to have a subset of all operations also like insert/remove at front and insert/remove at the end.It is typically implemented either using a doubly linked list or circular array. Common Operations of Deque:In order to make manipulations in a deque, there are certain operations provided to us.insertFront(x) → Insert an element at the front end.insertRear(x) → Insert an element at the rear end.deleteFront() → Delete an element from the front end.deleteRear() → Delete an element from the rear end.getFront() → Retrieve (but don’t remove) the front element.getRear() → Retrieve (but don’t remove) the rear element.isEmpty() → Check if the deque is empty.size() → Return the number of elements currently in the deque.Code Example \n            C++\n\n    #include <iostream>\n#include <deque>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    deque<int> dq;\n\n    dq.push_back(10);\n    dq.push_back(20);\n    dq.push_front(30);\n\n    // Print deque elements\n    for (int x : dq) cout << x << \" \";\n    cout << endl;\n\n    // Pop from front and back\n    dq.pop_front();\n    dq.pop_back();\n\n    // Print deque elements after pop\n    for (int x : dq) cout << x << \" \";\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n\n\n            Java\n\n    import java.util.ArrayDeque;\nimport java.util.Deque;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Deque<Integer> dq = new ArrayDeque<>();\n\n        dq.addLast(10);\n        dq.addLast(20);\n        dq.addFirst(30);\n\n        // Print deque elements\n        for (int x : dq) System.out.print(x + \" \");\n        System.out.println();\n\n        // Pop from front and back\n        dq.removeFirst();\n        dq.removeLast();\n\n        // Print deque elements after pop\n        for (int x : dq) System.out.print(x + \" \");\n    }\n}\n\n\n            Python\n\n    from collections import deque\n\ndq = deque()\n\ndq.append(10)\ndq.append(20)\ndq.appendleft(30)\n\n# Print deque elements\nprint(' '.join(map(str, dq)))\n\n# Pop from front and back\ndq.popleft()\ndq.pop()\n\n# Print deque elements after pop\nprint(' '.join(map(str, dq)))\n\n\n            C#\n\n    using System;\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\n\nclass Program {\n    static void Main() {\n        Deque<int> dq = new Deque<int>();\n\n        dq.AddLast(10);\n        dq.AddLast(20);\n        dq.AddFirst(30);\n\n        // Print deque elements\n        foreach (int x in dq) Console.Write(x + \" \");\n        Console.WriteLine();\n\n        // Pop from front and back\n        dq.RemoveFirst();\n        dq.RemoveLast();\n\n        // Print deque elements after pop\n        foreach (int x in dq) Console.Write(x + \" \");\n    }\n}\n\npublic class Deque<T> {\n    private LinkedList<T> list = new LinkedList<T>();\n\n    public void AddFirst(T value) { list.AddFirst(value); }\n    public void AddLast(T value) { list.AddLast(value); }\n    public void RemoveFirst() { list.RemoveFirst(); }\n    public void RemoveLast() { list.RemoveLast(); }\n    public IEnumerator<T> GetEnumerator() { return list.GetEnumerator(); }\n}\n\nOutput30 10 20 \n10 Implementation of Deque:Deque can be implemented in Different Ways :-Implementation of Deque Using ArrayImplementation of Deque Using LinkedListAdvantage of Deque:",
